              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to James H. Hanson, the legal question is whether Michigan\u2019s flat per\u2011truck fee is preempted by 49\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f14504 because it burdens interstate commerce."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8e8999892c840aa5892c4fa25de9b90ef9e7cb2289a2716dbd6d70a0fb8ad52d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8e8999892c84-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, another question is whether the fee can be structured as a $90 plating fee plus a $10 registration fee without violating the statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8e8999892c840aa5892c4fa25de9b90ef9e7cb2289a2716dbd6d70a0fb8ad52d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8e8999892c84-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice O'Connor, the Court also considered whether apportionment of the fee based on intrastate mileage is permissible."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8e8999892c840aa5892c4fa25de9b90ef9e7cb2289a2716dbd6d70a0fb8ad52d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8e8999892c84-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, the issue of whether a per\u2011vehicle fee applied regardless of usage is permissible was raised."
      }
    ],
