              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Digges, petitioners state that apportionment should reflect the taxpayer\u2019s activity in the state, not highway damage, and is a general revenue tax."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Digges",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8e8999892c840aa5892c4fa25de9b90ef9e7cb2289a2716dbd6d70a0fb8ad52d",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8e8999892c84-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 57,
                "start": 57
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Digges, petitioners note that out\u2011of\u2011state carriers would be disadvantaged by cumulative fees across states, leading to a balkanized commerce."
